<Base title="How BotMatch works" description="How BotPlanet's recommendation engine chooses a robot for you.">
  <h1>How BotMatch works</h1>
  <p class="muted" style="font-size:18px; max-width:680px;">BotMatch is a deterministic, auditable engine — the same answers always produce the same recommendation, and commission can never influence which product it picks.</p>

  <h2>1. You answer a few questions</h2>
  <p>Pool type, your main problem, what it should clean, power preference, budget and pool size. Nothing personal is required.</p>

  <h2>2. We score products on suitability only</h2>
  <p>Each product is scored on how well it fits your answers — cleaning coverage, power match, budget fit and pool-size capability. Products that can't work for you (wrong environment, too small for your pool, or the wrong <em>class</em> — a surface skimmer when you need a full clean) are excluded outright.</p>

  <h2>3. Then — and only then — we pick the best offer</h2>
  <p>After the product is chosen, we rank retailer offers by total price, delivery speed, warranty and how fresh the price data is. Commission is used only as a tie-break between offers that are otherwise equivalent — never to change the product.</p>

  <h2>4. Everything is recorded</h2>
  <p>Every recommendation stores your answers, the exact engine version, and the score of every candidate — so we can prove the recommendation was about fit, not money.</p>

  <p style="margin-top:26px;"><a class="btn primary" href="/botmatch/robotic-pool-cleaners/">Try BotMatch</a></p>
</Base>
